            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method and a decoder for error recovery in predictive coding of stereo or multichannel audio. A frame of consecutive frames of the received multichannel signal is decoded and responsive to receiving a previous frame bad frame indicator while operating in a predictive coding mode with a current frame of the consecutive frames, it is determined whether a parameter stability measure is below a threshold. Responsive to the parameter stability measure being below the threshold, stored decoded parameters are retrieved from a memory and the decoded parameters of the current frame are replaced with the retrieved parameters.</p>
            </abstract>
